<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n2309" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἰθέριος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">α</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, also <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ος</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>
		<i><span class="en">
			E.
			<u>Fr.</u>
			839.10
		</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
			Arist.
			<u>Mu.</u>
			392a31
		</span></i>:—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>of</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἰθήρ</span> or <i>the upper air</i>,
			hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b>
			<i>high in air, on high</i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Pr.</u>
				158
			</span></i> (anap.), <i><span class="en">
				<u>Th.</u>
				81
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>OC</u>
				1082
			</span></i>, etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἰθερία ἀνέπτα</span>
			flew up <i>into the air</i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Med.</u>
				440
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Andr.</u>
				830
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἰ. γῆ,</span> of the moon, <i><span class="en">
				Pythag.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Simp.
				<u>in Cael.</u>
				511.26
			</span></i>: epith. of Zeus, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Mu.</u>
				401a17
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>ethereal, heavenly</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φύσις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Parm.
					10.1
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἱ αἰ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hierocl.
					<u>in CA</u>
					27
				</span></i>
			 P.<i><span class="en">
				484M.
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γονή</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Fr.</u>
				</span></i>
			l.c. Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ίως</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Iamb.
					<u>Myst.</u>
					1.9
				</span></i>
			.—Trag. only in lyr.</div>
